<!-- SECTION: projects.Later -->
<section class="blk blk--ink u-block--ink" data-screen-label="Later">
  <div class="u-111 eyebrow">Later — studies &amp; demonstrations</div>
  <h2 class="u-112 sec">Gated on funding and safety.</h2>
  <p class="u-113 lead">Longer-term studies and partner-led physical demonstrations — greenhouses, filtration, solar, storage, circular materials — are treated as research and design tracks until there is funding, a local operator, safety review, legal capacity, insurance, and site permissions. None involves Uncost directly providing healthcare, care, child-facing education, or safety services.</p>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: projects.How they help -->
<section class="blk blk--cream" data-screen-label="How they help">
  <div class="eyebrow">The honest chain</div>
  <h2 class="u-114 sec">Every project has to earn its cost claim.</h2>
  <p class="u-108 lead">A project only counts as a cost-reduction path where energy, capital, maintenance, and local conditions make a net reduction plausible. Where the model shows it doesn&rsquo;t beat the status quo, we publish that negative result too. Where a cost driver is policy rather than technology, our role is open data and nonpartisan analysis — never partisan lobbying.</p>
</section>

